{"id":"api-github-review-write-flow-001","type":"api_behavior","fact":"GitHub MCP pull_request_review_write requires exactly 3 sequential calls to post a review with inline comments: (1) {method:'create'} to get a pending review id, (2) add_comment_to_pending_review once per inline finding, (3) {method:'submit', event:'COMMENT', body:'...'} to publish. Skipping create or submitting before adding comments results in a review with no inline annotations.","recommendation":"On any exception after step 1, call {method:'delete', reviewId: pendingId} to avoid orphaned pending reviews that block future review submissions. Store pendingReviewId before the loop and use it in the except/finally rollback.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"feature/003-inline-pr-comments — backend/services/code_review_service.py post_review_to_pull_request","date":"2026-06-16"}],"tags":["github","mcp","pull-request","code-review","api-flow"],"affectedFiles":["backend/services/code_review_service.py"],"affectedServices":["CodeReviewService","GitHubMCPClient"],"createdAt":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
